---
interface Props {
  kind: "future" | "ratings" | "meaning" | "routing";
}

const { kind } = Astro.props;

const ratings = [
  ["1", "Bobby Fischer", "USA", "2785"],
  ["2", "Boris Spassky", "USSR", "2660"],
  ["3=", "Tigran Petrosian", "USSR", "2645"],
  ["3=", "Lev Polugaevsky", "USSR", "2645"],
  ["5=", "Lajos Portisch", "Hungary", "2640"],
  ["5=", "Viktor Korchnoi", "USSR", "2640"],
  ["7=", "Mikhail Botvinnik", "USSR", "2630"],
  ["7=", "Anatoly Karpov", "USSR", "2630"],
  ["9=", "Bent Larsen", "Denmark", "2625"],
  ["9=", "Mikhail Tal", "USSR", "2625"],
];
---

{kind === "future" && (
  <figure class="fischer-figure fischer-figure--future article-wide not-prose" aria-labelledby="future-title future-caption">
    <header>
      <span>THE LOOK-AHEAD MYTH</span>
      <h3 id="future-title">Chess skill is not one long tunnel into the future.</h3>
    </header>
    <div class="future-tree" aria-hidden="true">
      <span class="future-tree__root">POSITION</span>
      <div class="future-tree__level future-tree__level--one">
        <span>forcing move</span><span>quiet move</span><span>bad move</span>
      </div>
      <div class="future-tree__lines future-tree__lines--one"></div>
      <div class="future-tree__level future-tree__level--two">
        <span>check</span><span>capture</span><span>threat</span><span class="muted">discard</span><span class="muted">discard</span>
      </div>
      <div class="future-tree__lines future-tree__lines--two"></div>
      <div class="future-tree__level future-tree__level--three">
        <span>compare</span><span>compare</span><span>compare</span><span>choose</span>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="figure-summary">PATTERN RECOGNITION + SELECTIVE SEARCH + EVALUATION</p>
    <figcaption id="future-caption">Strong players do not inspect every legal continuation. They recognize familiar structures, concentrate on promising candidates, and abandon branches that do not deserve more time.</figcaption>
  </figure>
)}

{kind === "ratings" && (
  <figure class="fischer-figure fischer-figure--ratings article-wide not-prose" aria-labelledby="ratings-title ratings-caption">
    <header>
      <span>JULY 1972 FIDE LIST</span>
      <h3 id="ratings-title">One American, seven Soviet players, and a 125-point gap.</h3>
    </header>
    <div class="ratings-table" role="table" aria-label="July 1972 FIDE top ten">
      <div class="ratings-table__row ratings-table__head" role="row">
        <span role="columnheader">Rank</span><span role="columnheader">Player</span><span role="columnheader">Federation</span><span role="columnheader">Rating</span>
      </div>
      {ratings.map(([rank, player, federation, rating], index) => (
        <div class:list={["ratings-table__row", { "ratings-table__row--fischer": index === 0 }]} role="row">
          <span role="cell">{rank}</span><strong role="cell">{player}</strong><span role="cell">{federation}</span><b role="cell">{rating}</b>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
    <figcaption id="ratings-caption">Fischer entered the Reykjavík match as world number one. The Soviet system still occupied seven of the other nine positions in the published top ten.</figcaption>
  </figure>
)}

{kind === "meaning" && (
  <figure class="fischer-figure fischer-figure--meaning article-wide not-prose" aria-labelledby="meaning-title meaning-caption">
    <header>
      <span>THREE PUBLIC STORIES</span>
      <h3 id="meaning-title">The board stayed put. The metaphor kept changing.</h3>
    </header>
    <ol class="meaning-cards">
      <li>
        <span>1972</span>
        <strong>Nation against nation</strong>
        <p>Fischer and Spassky become a Cold War contest that general-interest television can explain to a mass audience.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span>1997</span>
        <strong>Human against machine</strong>
        <p>Kasparov and Deep Blue turn chess into a public test of what computation can take from human expertise.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span>Now</span>
        <strong>Player inside a network</strong>
        <p>Championships, streams, clips, engines, creators, and millions of daily games coexist without requiring one national doorway.</p>
      </li>
    </ol>
    <figcaption id="meaning-caption">Each era used chess to tell a larger story about the system it was trying to understand.</figcaption>
  </figure>
)}

{kind === "routing" && (
  <figure class="fischer-figure fischer-figure--routing article-wide not-prose" aria-labelledby="routing-title routing-caption">
    <header>
      <span>FAME IS A DELIVERY SYSTEM</span>
      <h3 id="routing-title">One public room became millions of private routes.</h3>
    </header>
    <div class="routing-grid">
      <section>
        <span>Broadcast television</span>
        <strong>One guest</strong>
        <div class="routing-flow routing-flow--broadcast" aria-hidden="true">
          <i>network</i><b>→</b><i>scheduled show</i><b>→</b><i>national audience</i>
        </div>
        <p>Scarcity concentrated attention. A specialist could become a household name because many households received the same invitation.</p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <span>Personalized platforms</span>
        <strong>Many chess publics</strong>
        <div class="routing-flow routing-flow--network" aria-hidden="true">
          <i>games</i><i>streams</i><i>shorts</i><i>news</i><i>engines</i><i>archives</i>
        </div>
        <p>Abundance distributes attention. A player can be enormous inside chess and nearly absent from the next person’s feed.</p>
      </section>
    </div>
    <figcaption id="routing-caption">Modern chess does not lack an audience. It lacks the old requirement that unrelated audiences pass through the same few channels.</figcaption>
  </figure>
)}

<style>
  .fischer-figure {
    --paper: #eee2c9;
    --ink: #121719;
    --red: #bc492d;
    --blue: #345a70;
    --gold: #d19a48;
    margin-block: 2.8rem !important;
    padding: clamp(1rem, 3vw, 1.7rem);
    overflow: hidden;
    border: 1px solid rgb(37 31 23 / 0.25);
    border-radius: 0.28rem;
    background:
      radial-gradient(circle at 12% 15%, rgb(255 255 255 / 0.55), transparent 25%),
      repeating-linear-gradient(0deg, transparent 0 9px, rgb(91 70 45 / 0.025) 9px 10px),
      var(--paper);
    color: var(--ink);
    box-shadow: 0.65rem 0.72rem 0 rgb(31 24 18 / 0.16);
  }

  header {
    margin-bottom: 1.3rem;
    text-align: left;
  }

  header span {
    color: var(--red);
    font: 800 0.64rem/1.2 var(--font-mono), monospace;
    letter-spacing: 0.15em;
  }

  header h3 {
    margin: 0.3rem 0 0 !important;
    color: var(--ink);
    font-size: clamp(1.2rem, 3.1vw, 1.75rem) !important;
    line-height: 1.08 !important;
  }

  figcaption {
    margin: 1rem 0 0 !important;
    padding-top: 0.85rem;
    border-top: 1px solid rgb(18 23 25 / 0.22);
    color: #574f43;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
    text-align: left !important;
  }

  .future-tree {
    position: relative;
    display: grid;
    gap: 1.55rem;
    padding: 0.5rem 0;
  }

  .future-tree__root,
  .future-tree__level span {
    position: relative;
    z-index: 1;
    display: block;
    padding: 0.46rem 0.55rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--ink);
    background: #f8efd9;
    font: 700 0.64rem/1.2 var(--font-mono), monospace;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .future-tree__root {
    justify-self: center;
    width: min(11rem, 70%);
    border-color: var(--red);
    background: var(--ink);
    color: #fff7e5;
  }

  .future-tree__level {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.55rem;
  }

  .future-tree__level--one { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); }
  .future-tree__level--two { grid-template-columns: repeat(5, 1fr); }
  .future-tree__level--three { grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr); }

  .future-tree__level .muted {
    border-style: dashed;
    opacity: 0.45;
    text-decoration: line-through;
  }

  .future-tree::before,
  .future-tree::after {
    position: absolute;
    left: 8%;
    right: 8%;
    height: 1px;
    background: var(--red);
    content: "";
  }

  .future-tree::before { top: 4.3rem; }
  .future-tree::after { top: 8.9rem; background: var(--blue); }

  .figure-summary {
    margin: 0.85rem 0 0 !important;
    color: var(--blue);
    font: 800 0.7rem/1.4 var(--font-mono), monospace;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .ratings-table {
    border: 1px solid var(--ink);
  }

  .ratings-table__row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 3rem minmax(0, 1.5fr) minmax(5rem, 0.8fr) 4rem;
    align-items: center;
    min-height: 2.25rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgb(18 23 25 / 0.18);
  }

  .ratings-table__row:last-child { border-bottom: 0; }
  .ratings-table__row > * { padding: 0.38rem 0.55rem; }
  .ratings-table__row strong { font-size: 0.78rem; }
  .ratings-table__row span,
  .ratings-table__row b { font: 700 0.66rem/1.2 var(--font-mono), monospace; }
  .ratings-table__head { background: var(--ink); color: #fff4dc; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .ratings-table__row--fischer { background: var(--red); color: white; }

  .meaning-cards {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 0.75rem;
    margin: 0 !important;
    padding: 0 !important;
    list-style: none;
  }

  .meaning-cards li {
    display: grid;
    align-content: start;
    gap: 0.45rem;
    min-height: 13rem;
    margin: 0 !important;
    padding: 1rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--ink);
    background: #f8efd9;
  }

  .meaning-cards li:nth-child(2) { background: var(--ink); color: #fff2d8; }
  .meaning-cards span { color: var(--red); font: 900 1.65rem/1 var(--font-mono), monospace; }
  .meaning-cards strong { font-size: 1rem; line-height: 1.15; }
  .meaning-cards p { margin: 0 !important; font-size: 0.72rem; line-height: 1.5; }
  .meaning-cards li:nth-child(2) p { color: #cfc5b1; }

  .routing-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 0.8rem;
  }

  .routing-grid section {
    display: grid;
    align-content: start;
    gap: 0.55rem;
    padding: 1rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--ink);
    background: #f8efd9;
  }

  .routing-grid section > span { color: var(--red); font: 800 0.62rem/1.2 var(--font-mono), monospace; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .routing-grid section > strong { font-size: 1.12rem; }
  .routing-grid section > p { margin: 0 !important; font-size: 0.74rem; line-height: 1.55; }

  .routing-flow {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.35rem;
    align-items: center;
    margin-block: 0.45rem;
  }

  .routing-flow i {
    padding: 0.33rem 0.42rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--blue);
    background: #e6d9bd;
    font: 700 0.6rem/1.2 var(--font-mono), monospace;
    font-style: normal;
  }

  .routing-flow--network {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
  }

  .routing-flow--network i:nth-child(even) { border-color: var(--red); }

  @media (max-width: 42rem) {
    .meaning-cards,
    .routing-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .meaning-cards li { min-height: 0; }
  }

  @media (max-width: 32rem) {
    .fischer-figure { padding: 0.8rem; }
    .future-tree__level--two { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); }
    .ratings-table__row { grid-template-columns: 2.5rem minmax(0, 1.4fr) 4.6rem 3.6rem; }
    .ratings-table__row > * { padding-inline: 0.3rem; }
    .ratings-table__row span,
    .ratings-table__row b { font-size: 0.57rem; }
    .ratings-table__row strong { font-size: 0.68rem; }
  }
</style>
